// Library / SDK trust boundary — public-API parameter sources.
//
// A reusable library has no single entry point: any caller may pass attacker-controlled
// data through a public API. So a function/method PARAMETER that flows unsanitized into a
// sink (SQL, command, LDAP filter, HTML render, file path, …) is a real vulnerability in
// library code. `source param` is a first-class source form (like `source method` /
// `source receiver`) that labels parameter nodes.
//
// Gated by the trust boundary: code.ExternalEntryInput is an ACTIVE source ONLY under the
// `library` profile (profiles/library.vyql). The parameter-source adapter is default-OFF —
// under application profiles, and with no profile, parameters are never sources, so apps
// are unaffected. cross_language: parameters exist in every frontend.
adapter library {
  meta { fidelity: syntactic, cross_language: true, auto_apply: graph }

  source param -> code.ExternalEntryInput
}
